A||||50||TRiAD||Rant. (Sorry, you don't have to read it, but I have to say it.)||||9||
Z||000000||TRiAD||11-21-2001||11:36 PM||||I'm VERY disappointed and upset. <P>I sold a car that worked fine, in order to buy this Fiero (that I was told also worked fine). Now, less than 300 miles later, it is completely inoperable, and I'm out the money and viable transportation. <P>I was told the following things would be fixed before I picked it up;<BR>* windshield (totally cracked, $250)<BR>* headliner (another $250)<BR>* headlamps (they were mostly fixed)<BR>...other than the headlamps (the dricer's side one sticks UP) the rest was untouched when I arrived, driving 3 hours away to pick up the car. <BR>I was told I could borrow plates to get home, then that I couldn't, but that a "temp" tag would be OK, and they're "free", (then the seller and his friend ditch me at the DMV where it later becomes known that I have to pay $12.75 for the temp tag.) <BR>After I agree to the price, and PAY for the car, as the title is being signed, I notice that the odometer reading is listed on the title as "not actual miles". The seller gave NO warning of this, even listing the miles of the car in his "ad" (in a thread here). (Mind you, we've agreed on price, and the money has changed hands already).<BR>So, at that point I am a little disappointed, but I have my Fiero, and I'm all excited. It's tough to shift, but aren't all 4 speeds? So I get it home, detail it, and take LOTS of pics, and it keeps getting harder to shift. I get pulled over for the LOUD exhaust (you can't tell from the driver's seat, the seller never mentioned it, either) and am told to remove the window tint (neither here nor there, but anyone know how to get the glue off? Alcohol didn't work.), and it keeps getting harder to shift. <BR>Finally, it gets to the point where it won't even shift when the engine is running, and it "creeps" really bad when you have it in gear, even if the pedal is to the floor. <BR>I ask around, and am told it's either<BR>* aluminum clutch pedal ($30, but taking forever to get it here from Twin Lakes)<BR>* clutch cylinder(s) ($250 ea)<BR>* clutch ($700)<P>I WAS planning a 5sp Isuzu swap ($1500 complete) anyway, so I'm trying to get the pedal first, just hoping it will work for a while, because all the rest would be replaced in the trans swap, and it would be expensive and redundant to replace it twice.<P>NOW, my situation is critical. I have a wife and 2 kids, now we only have one car (which needs some work) and because of the $2,150 I spent on this car (which doesn't work) and some other circumstances (most of which the seller knew), I'm in VERY dire straits. <BR>I had an awesome job offer last week, but someone with more experience applied late, and got it. (I'm hoping for nother one SOON)<P>So now, the Supercharger project is postponed (indefinitely), any other mods to the car are also postponed, and I will have to count myself as VERY blessed if I can even afford to get this car running again. <P>I feel like the seller (who said since he's a Mormon, he's bound to always be honest, and since I was "a good guy" that he was going to "take better care" of me than he would some schmoe he didn't know) <BR>...was more than a little misleading, and downright dishonest in his description of the car, the situation with the items that were supposed to be fixed, and the temp tags (now the least of my worries) especially the miles, and the clutch situation. <BR>I hate to put it that way, but I feel like I've been royally screwed and taken advantage of by another forum member. (Some of you know who he is, I will NOT give his name, if he responds, it is his will to be disclosed.)<P>How do we fix the situation? Well, I'm sure he's disinterested in any action on his part, and Lord knows I can't afford to sue him. <BR>What would I like to see? Well, if the pedal gets it back on the road (if it ever arrives, he said yesterday he hadn't even removed it yet!) I'll be satisfied with an apology, and forwarning on any other known gremlins. If it's bigger? Maybe a partial refund would be the honest thing to do. I don't know. <BR>What do I expect? At the most, a flaming rebukation in response from the seller. He may not even respond, since it's obvious he was dishonest, especially in regards to the mileage. That's just like a "junk" title, IMHO. I certainly don't ecpect any "good-will", given his record so far. <P>Anyway, this is my first Fiero, and I'm determined to get it running and make it worth every penny I put into it, if I can get the finances flowing again soon. If anyone has any help they can offer (advice, a steel clutch pedal, maybe a cheap shop manual) I'd seriously be VERY grateful.<BR> <BR>I'm stuck down here in Central Illinois, the Chicago people are too far away, and the car came from Indiana, so I don't feel like there's any way to get any personal assistance with any of this...I kinda feel all alone in this, you know?<P>I appreciate an open forum where I can vent my frustrations, if it weren't unkind, I'd be more detailed and less constrained. <BR>I also really appreciate all the help I've had so far, and the fact that there's a place like this were that can happen. <P>Thanks.<P>[adytod bikewz aye quen't speel]<p>[This message has been edited by TRiAD (edited 11-21-2001).]||||reg||9
Z||000001||yo_sweet||11-21-2001||11:46 PM||||I feel for you man i alomst bought an 85 GT with aftermarket t-tops for $500 canadian it supposidly had 90k on it i got the buyers pakage  and the it had 234k from the last owner before the guy who was selling it!, none the less i passed! som people are just plain unloyal these days ,its hard to find a good trusting person to deal with in the big cities even if he seems like a nice guy, my uncle traded his 1973 vette for a 1989 iroc convertible it turns out the car was registered to a 86 2.8 camero the vin on the dash  was way off to the one on the inside of the quarter panel , the guy that he bought it off of basicly told him to go **** himself! when he approched him , now he's stuck with a bad title on a car that needs a full resto!, i hope you get what you desirve man!<P>||||reg||13
Z||000002||loafer87gt||11-22-2001||12:06 AM||||Quick question about your transmission, does the problem go away after your car has been running for a while. I know in winter I used to have tranny problems with my 5 speeds and it turned out a had a crack in the cover around my shifter cables and ice was getting in there. Eventually the heat from the engine would thaw them out though and I could shift OK. If thats not the case, it could very well be the slave or master cylinder. Sorry to hear about your bad luck, I'm sure a lot of forum members have had similar experiences. The Fiero is an absolute blast to drive when its running, but a real *****  when things start acting up, it always seems like they when one thing goes everything goes along with it. Heres hoping you get everything worked out, ||||reg||1
Z||000003||TRiAD||11-22-2001||12:12 AM||||warm weather in IL so far, but thanks! I wish it were that easy.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Neal||11-22-2001||12:13 AM||||Have you bled the clutch hydraulics, and I mean bleed and bleed some more, using archies method and any other tricks you can.<P>it sounds like that may help your clutch problem||||reg||1
Z||000005||TRiAD||11-22-2001||12:15 AM||||can you email me those instructions? I'm new to all this. Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Dave Gunsul||11-22-2001||12:43 AM||||Sorry to hear about all your troubles Triad.<BR>Your first Fiero should be a happy experience<BR>and not a bad one. Sometimes I wonder if there's any good left in the world anymore.<BR>It seems people are just out for themselves and they don't give a flying fingernail about anybody else. That's a shame.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>I hope your luck changes for the better!<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||9
Z||000007||TRiAD||11-22-2001||12:57 AM||||He has emailed me. We're taking that conversation to email...<P>I will keep everyone posted on my progress with the car. <P>[edit]it will be slow...[edit]<p>[This message has been edited by TRiAD (edited 11-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Monkeyman||11-22-2001||01:37 AM||||Triad--You can get a windshield replaced for less than $200.  I'll dig around and see what the name of the company was who quoted me the price.  A brand new fiberglass headliner board from the FS will run you less than $200 also.  The cost for the material to cover it in inconsequential.  A clutch replacement shouldn't cost more than about $550 (at the local dealership, no less).  Don't give up on Bob Stieger.  He'll ship it.  Sometimes it takes a little while if he's swamped, but he's always come through for me.<P>I feel your pain.  I bought a Fiero (2 or 3 Fieros ago) from a forum member.  There were a number of problems I wasn't informed about.  It got to the point where the car wasn't drivable (my only transportation).  Fortunately, with a little credit from the local dealership (Dorais Chevy in Wabash--great guys), I was able to get it fixed.  I was owed some parts (dew wipes) the never made it to me.  I finally bought some new ones.  A few months later, the seller told me he would send me a check to cover the cost.  I've never seen the check, BTW.  I think the worst part is that he's friends with another forum member and now he won't speak to me either.  (I can only guess it's because of the seller, but I could be wrong.)  I won't mention the sellers name because I don't feel like starting a war.  (If anyone knows whom I'm referring to, please keep it to yourself.)  On the other hand, if you tell me which forum member bent you over, I'll send my cousin Bruno the Fist to his house to rearrange his kneecaps. (j/k)<P>Best of luck getting your car fixed.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/patriot.gif">    <BR><B><FONT COLOR="red">Proud</FONT> <FONT COLOR="white">to be an</FONT> <FONT COLOR="blue">American</FONT>!!</B>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Neal||11-22-2001||01:40 AM||||email sent||||reg||1
Z||000010||JohnnyK||11-22-2001||02:23 AM||||Since it kept getting harder and harder to shift, it is either the master cylinder, slave cylinder, or line. It is NOT the actual clutch (it might be worn down too, btu thats unrelated), and bleeding it won't help (well, it will temporarily, but you will get the same slow deterioration) (Yes, most people diagnose clutch problems as a Bleeding Problem). Either way, if it started better, and slowly kept getting worse, it is a cylinder or line problem.||||reg||1
Z||000011||JohnnyK||11-22-2001||02:24 AM||||I repeat, unless it's slipping (I only read the top of your post), it is the hydraulics/linkage (needs something replaced, not a bleeding), not the actual clutch.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Flamberge||11-22-2001||02:58 AM||||One possible way out of the bad-car mess is to try to get it IM'ed. If it fails, then you have a right to demand a refund on the car. (At least in TX and AK.) Also, isn't there a full-refund grace period in most states for used car sales to protect the buyer? Like 5 days or something...? Find out FAST, Triad. <P>Also, try contacting the seller. He might not even know about the mileage. My old red Fiero (do a search under my name and look for the one with "Pics" in the title) when I sold it to help pay for my 88GT, the people who bought it from me when to get the title in their name and the DMV told them it was a *salvage* title. I had no idea. So I called the guy I bought the car from, he had no idea, and through some investigative work I was able to call the guy *he* bought it from, back in 1993. That guy returned my call, strangely enough, but I haven't been able to get in contact with him since. I agreed to have the buyer of my red Fiero just call it even on what they owed me (I ended up selling it for $900 instead of the $1500 we agreed on.) I felt/feel terrible for the salvage title. I wouldn't even want the car if I was them.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> They only bought it from me in the first place because I let them make monthly payments of $300. (And I am Mormon too, btw. If they really *were* LDS, why would they bring that up as a selling point?)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"> I am *hoping* that if they are LDS, that they would be willing to work with you on the car. If you contacted them, maybe they could work something out. And if they won't, then I would maybe try to get the DMV (or someone) involved. The used car buyer has rights, Triad. I am behind you 100%. Please keep us updated.<P>------------------<BR>- Flamberge<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://flamberge.iwarp.com/Serra3sm.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||maryjane||11-22-2001||08:41 AM||||Here in Texas, I believe the "not actual mileage" means it has rolled over" Is that what you're talking about? Sorry to hear about your problems, I agree with Johhny about the clutch problem & I remember several windshield threads from the tech section-they quoted prices a lot cheaper than you mentioned, but guess it depends on your locale. Get someone to run carfax to find any outright mis-representations. If you can't get any results from the seller, maybe the 'threat' of a lawsuit will prompt results, I dunno. A lot of law firms offer a free 'first consultation', if it comes to that. Good luck to ya. Here are 2 links to lemon laws, the first one has a free carfax button at the bottom (I didn't try it).The second one has info on buying used cars. There are others listed under a google search "lemon laws" as search name, with quotations. <A HREF="http://autopedia.com/html/HotLinks_LemonState.html" TARGET=_blank>http://autopedia.com/html/HotLinks_LemonState.html</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.carlemon.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.carlemon.com/</A> <p>[This message has been edited by maryjane (edited 11-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000014||Jake_Dragon||11-22-2001||09:38 AM||||Decal remover should take off the glue, look for it in a spray can.<BR>Sorry to hear about your problems.<BR>Take a break, I know it can be hard to do but a good cleansing breath will allow you to focus on what you really want to do.<BR>I got took on my SC and could have made them take it back, didn't because I wanted the car too much. I fixed most of the problems with it. After clearing my head and finding out what it would take to get my car back on the road I felt it was worth what I paid for it. <P>You need to decide if you got what you paid for.<P>Wish you the best of luck.<P><P>------------------<BR>          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/left.gif">                        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_brow.gif">                       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/right.gif">           <BR>               <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gt2_3.GIF"> ||||reg||1
Z||000015||Jaygee79||11-22-2001||09:41 AM||||i don't know if your state is one of them, but some states have Lemon Laws.  you might want to check into it.||||reg||1
Z||000016||TRiAD||11-22-2001||09:53 AM||||Thanks again, all...<BR>A couple things; I've contacted the seller, he says he was honest about the car, and that I must have broken something (although he mentioned in my thread in the tech section that he had the same problem once, weeks ago, and it went away; something else he never mentioned before). <BR>(He even told me once that the GTech won't fit the lighter; then later he told me he ran like a 15.0 1/4 mile. I decided to see if my GTech would fit the plug, and it doesn't...)<BR>As for "rolling over", our cars have a 100,000 space, and the car's registering like 92K right now (which is what the seller told me it had). He now says that he told me that was actual mileage...I'm not sure how that helps, that's the problem, it's not actual mileage. Huh...The gauges are falling beloe the holes for them in the fascia, and are resting on the steering column. The oil gauge is dead as well. Didn't notice till I got home. <P>Anyway, I'll try the bleeding thing (after checking the cylinders and lines) and after replacing the pedal. <P>As for follow up, I know LDSs are big on honesty and righteousness, so I'll leave it to his sense of right and wrong. I'm not going to have a lawyer send him a letter, because I have no intention  of pursuing it. I do believe he intentionally misrepresented the car, but it's too much trouble to try to make it right, especially over state lines. <BR>I do not expect him to make it right. <P>Jake, I definitely did not get $2,150 worth of car, any car, but I have already decided that I am going to get it on the road. <P>Thanks for all your help!<BR><p>[This message has been edited by TRiAD (edited 11-22-2001).]||||reg||1
