Z||000019||isthiswhereiputausername?||11-22-2001||10:42 AM||||Sorry to hear about your hassles  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>I would suggest that you check the clutch slave to see if its bent (fork might be loose or worn)<P>what was wrong with the headliner that was in it? <P><BR>Good luck!<P>||||reg||9
Z||000020||Voytek||11-22-2001||10:49 AM||||Sorry to hear about the problems.<P>Just one thing.<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>I know LDSs are big on honesty and righteousness, so I'll leave it to his sense of right and wrong<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I would re-word that and say '...claim they are big on honesty...'<BR>There is no such thing for most people in today's world.  I have a LDS neighbor.  He can quote the bible like not many people.  He is also pirating 2 satellite systems and doesn't give it a second thought.  He's gone to pretty great lengths to get the local satellite system for free.<P>Now I'm no saint either (with the satellite thing).  On the other hand, I am selling my '85 SE and have been working on some minor and less minor things for the last 2 weeks so I can sell it with clear concience -the car will be as good as new.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Nothing against LDS members.  It's just the way it is today - can't trust most people, no matter what they claim to be.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000021||DaRkLoRD||11-22-2001||01:03 PM||||Hey TRiAD, sorry to hear about the fiero problems.. I had some "fun" experiences with a Fiero I bought as well, about 2 months ago... at lest you still have yours.<P>Anyway, there's some great people on here.. I have no doubt that you'll receive all the help you need in getting the fiero working great!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000022||TRiAD||11-22-2001||01:21 PM||||Yeah, Voytek, when I told him how much money I spent on the car I was selling, he didn't understand...Why spend that much on what is essentially someone else's car? Because I too, wanted to sell it with a clear conscience. <P>Darklord, I have gotten a few very helpful emails, in addition to the advice on this thread. I hope it will all work out. <P>Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000023||Neverfinished||11-22-2001||03:33 PM||||Is your clutch pedal right to the ground when you shift??<BR>when i first bought my 84 se 4 speed it hurt my foot because i had to push down so hard.<P>I simple bit of welding will cure the problem if that is it. Also align your shifter maybe...<P>also VOYTEK do you have a buyer for your se??<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000024||Master_Sushi||11-22-2001||06:02 PM||||Geting screwed really sucks. When its on a big thing like a car its even worse. I sold my 88 coupe a few months ago. I was honest with everything, pointed out every prob, answered every question 100% honestly. I was probably too honest infact, if I lied about a few things I probably could have got 300$ more for the car. But I can't stand lieing!<P>Good luck fixing the car! Don't give up and don't get mad.||||reg||1
Z||000025||JohnnyK||11-22-2001||06:05 PM||||Triad.. don't even both bleeding the clutch, it will be fine for a few days/weeks/month and then go bad again. Course, I still haven't bothered to fix mine, so it's sitting dead in the driveway.. someone come get it..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000026||Voytek||11-22-2001||06:42 PM||||Hey Neverfinished<BR>No, I haven't started advertising yet.  It's going to the paper next week.<P>From what you told me, I'm not sure that this is what you'd be looking for.<P>This one is an '85 SE V6 Auto - white, base coupe body style.  Only 134,000 kms.  Really nice shape and good tires but quite basic (only has speakers in the headrests, tilt wheel, GM stereo and power trunk release).  No mods, all original.<P>Due to fairly low mileage and new parts (e-brake lines, timing cover gasket, oil pan gasket, water pump gasket, main bearing seal) I will be asking $3500 CDN - hoping to get about $3000 out of it.<P>Not that anyone from the US is going to buy it, but for those of you who are American it's about $1900 USD.||||reg||1
Z||000027||The Fieromaster||11-22-2001||07:39 PM||||If you still havent got the tranny thing solved get ahold of Fieromaster88 on here OR in Aol (aol instant messanger/buddy list) he goes by the same name... he had the same problem with his tranny and got it all worked out now it shifts like a honda... smooth as hell with a LIGHT clutch feeling!<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">         <FONT COLOR="red">"Raced That, Wrecked Better"</FONT>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">      <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif"">                 <BR><B>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000</B><BR><FONT COLOR="blue"><B>AIM: Fieromaster</B></FONT><BR><B><FONT COLOR="purple">1985 GT ~ Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="maroon">1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX ~ Maroon w/ Hella Balls!(GSX = AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="green">1992 Mitsubishi Eclipse GS ~ soon will be turboed</FONT><BR></B>||||reg||1
Z||000028||Sootah||11-22-2001||07:44 PM||||You think <B>YOU</B> were screwed!! I bought my 85 GT and threw a rod 40 miles out of town!! When I checked the oil b4 I left town it was a perfect honey color. I didn't think anything of this. 40 miles out of town rod knocks, then rapidly ejects itself.<P>When I finally get the car towed home (had to rent a trailer for this) I check the oil. It's nice and chrome now, not to mention black as hell. I guarentee that he bought the car (said it was a restore project) changed the oil, saw that it was all chromed out and said to himself 'holy god, better get out of this car hella fast'. He then puts in a thicker oil to keep the rod knock away until the car gets up to temp.<P>Anyway, I called the guy and GUESS WHAT, he wants nothing to do with it. 'I don't know what you did to it after you left'. Even though WHAT IN GOD'S NAME COULD I HAVE DONE?!?!? I ONLY GOT 40 MILES OUT OF TOWN!! Shìt.<P>Well, now I am looking at better than $1800 in repair bills. Need to buy a rebuilt engine and have somebody put it in. The guy that was helping me with the swap fell through so now I have to pay somebody. This I don't have $ for. I need to get a loan. Oh, wait... I DON'T HAVE ANY CREDIT!! I'm 19 and never had a credit card or loan b4. I can't get one without a co-signer. Everybody that <I>would</I> sign with me is strapped, and the other option is a self-righteous bastard. (I also am a Mormon, but have decided against going on a mission. Dad is all guilt-trip giving about this now. Even though its better for me not to go at all than to go and come home after a couple months)<P>What I'm getting at TRiAD is I feel for ya. Your not the only one in this boat...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__Nuclear_Happy_Face_Sig.jpg">        <BR><sup><A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__Black_Beauty_-_Front_Right.jpg" TARGET=_blank>The Black Beauty</A> (85 GT) - <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__Busted-Ass_SE.jpg" TARGET=_blank>Bustedato</A> (86 SE, Parts car)<BR><I>Never pull your pants down in Cosco, the dang monkeys will getcha</I></sup> <BR><sup><B>AIM</B>: KSSouter<BR><B>MSN IM</B>: I_R_Sootah@hotmail.com<BR></sup>||||reg||1
Z||000029||Mach10||11-22-2001||07:46 PM||||Triad: You been screwed. Don't just leave it up to his sense of right and wrong. Although it's nice to see that some people have faith in humanity (quoth Mach10 the cynicist), the fact remains: He's buggered you. LDS or not. He's still a human being, and therefore has the same capacity for serpentine back-stabbing as any of the other snake mo'fos on this planet  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Check out the lemon-laws. The odo thing is pretty much fraud there and then. Ask him to PROVE that you broke it etc.<P>Sorry to say it, but you might be SOL. So, Bleed the clutch (hey, if it lasts 2 weeks, that's 2 more weeks to find the parts  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">), and try the cheap temporary solutions until you can afford to fix it, permanently  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||4
Z||000030||TRiAD||11-22-2001||10:04 PM||||Thanks again, all. Sorry to hear that some of you have been in the same situation, but it does help net feeling quite so alone. <P>I especially appreciate those who have been discussing religion with me in other threads (you know who you are) who are in my court here...that shows bags of integrity in my book. <P>I'm going to try the pedal, examine the cylinders and hydraulics, and go from there...<P>Thanks again!||||reg||1
Z||000031||Mach10||11-22-2001||10:20 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by TRiAD:<BR><B>Thanks again, all. Sorry to hear that some of you have been in the same situation, but it does help net feeling quite so alone. <P>I especially appreciate those who have been discussing religion with me in other threads (you know who you are) who are in my court here...that shows bags of integrity in my book. <P>I'm going to try the pedal, examine the cylinders and hydraulics, and go from there...<P>Thanks again!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Put things in perspective. Whatever differences or arguments we have in other posts, it should have NO bearing elsewhere... You'll still get ANY help that I could offer. <P>We're a fambly, here... Fogeddaboutit!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||10
Z||000032||artherd||11-23-2001||02:36 AM||||Often someone discovers something *really* wrong with their car, and decides to SELL it and get something that runs...<P>The thing here is wether you sell your car "Fiero: has rod knock, tranny and chassis good"  or "<P>I've only been mislead about a car once, I talked and emailed with a nice gent about his Formula, paid for it, and *then* flew 800 miles one-way to pick it up and drive it back!<P>Car made the trip just fine, all as advertised.   However, it had no Air Conditioning.  Seller told me in email that it did (when listing options) but nope!<P>I didn't ever think anything of it in our discussions (who would?) and since I wanted to try something different with climate controls (thermostat control eg.  Mercedes, newer cars) anyway, AND since I had an 87 parts car with a (mostly) working AC, the point was and is basically moot.<P>Never even mentioned it to the guy, I was too busy enjoying the 88  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>It all worked out for the best, I'm 'forced' to do the cool custom AC thing that I wanted to do anyway, and now I have an excuse!<P>Triad:  Maybe TRY to think of this as a blessing.  It sucks to be withought transportation majorly, but you now DO have an excuse to swap in a good tranny and to rebuild all the junk that's marginal on the car.    The one great thing about Fieros is that you can buy one, overpay, have it break, dump a BUTTLOAD of money into it fixing it better than it ever was new, all for far far far less than the purchase price of any new, and most used, cars.<P>PS: I thought you had your own Speed Shop?<P>PPS: Email me about Corbelu Carrera seats  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000033||Neal||11-23-2001||03:02 AM||||i still say try bleeding the clutch, against johnny k's advice, say it works for a month, well you now have a vehicle for a month, and youve narrowed the source down to ONLY the hydroulics.<P>Much better than wondering about the rest of the system.  Plus you can keep rebleeding the system for a while, keep fluid a wrench and the mity vac in the car... (nope no experience there, honest, i swear... Oh nevermind)<P>Also if the shifter is stiff (regardless of anything else) you may want to try new shifter cables.  It worked for me, but then again the select cable was cracked the entire area of the engine bay...||||reg||1
Z||000034||Flamberge||11-23-2001||04:26 AM||||I agree with the other LDS comments on this thread to an extent. Everyone is human, but I think what he did (sell a lemon to you) is completely wrong, and not justifiable in any way to him. If he lied about the car, he probably lied about being LDS. (I hope so, "Mormons" are sometimes misunderstood and sometimes disliked because of people like that jerk! *sigh* Oh well. If it is any consolation, I tried as best as I could to correct the problem I had with the salvage title and the buyer, and they were as satisfied as could be expected in the process. And your car is worth WAY less than $2150!!! At least in its condition. To put it in perspective, look at my signature. I bought that car (88GT) 6 months ago for $2400. Single owner/garage-kept/fully loaded. My 85 Fiero I sold for $1500 and got 900 because of the salvage title fiasco. (why wouldn't the word "salvage" appear on a salvage title anywhere?! It just had a tiny "*S*" in the corner of the title.) Sounds like you should have paid about $500 for that car, man.<P>Sorry again.<P> <P>------------------<BR>- Flamberge<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://flamberge.iwarp.com/Serra3sm.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000035||Sootah||11-23-2001||01:22 PM||||Now <B>that</B> is where I lucked out. I only paid $800 for mine. Body perfect, interior only has a couple of easily fixed flaws. I may have been screwed, but not gang raped.<P>As for the LDS thing, we can be just a cruel and corrupt as the rest of humanity. If he was using that as a sales ploy then I'd have become suspicious rather quickly. It does, however, suprise me that a non-Utah mormon would do this. Utah mormons are seriously the worst ones on the planet. The reason behind this would be that we are raised surrounded by our fellow kin, we see them make mistakes and so its easier for the rest of us to. Non Utahn's see their friends make mistakes but then think 'well he's a baptist, so he's held to a different standard than I'<P>Anyway, I've had many an argument about that. I'm right, just trust me. (Me being a mormon in Utah and all that) As soon as somebody says 'I'm a ______ so I <I>have</I> to be honest', run the other way. Truely religous people never use that as leverage.<P>Kinda sucks, I know who on the forum sold it to you and I get along w/ him quite well. Probably still will. You must also realize that he may <I>not</I> have known there was anything major wrong with the car. Unlike my sale...<P><B>PEACE <I>-Sootah</B></I><P><B>EDIT</B>: I R cant not spel wurth sheeeit.<p>[This message has been edited by Sootah (edited 11-23-2001).]||||reg||1
