Z||000047||westtexas||11-26-2001||08:23 AM||||Triad,<P>A year ago this weekend I bought (sight-unseen) a '86 GT off ebay with only 54,000 original miles. Didn't know a thing about Fiero's, just that the GT looked great. When a got in to drive it home, had a hard time getting in first. Ground in every gear. When I got home I was so mad I didn't drive it for three weeks. The car was sold on ebay as being perfect. He knew the driveline had  problems. With the help of internet Fiero fanatics I changed the chutch pedal but found that the trans only had a pint of fluid. Seals were gone and the ignorant/thieving seller, who bought a Honda Civic, didn't mention the oil pools he must of seen when it was parked. The synchros barely work now with GM synchromesh. I often wonder what it would be like to drive with a real transmission. <P>The rest of the story: many years ago I traded in a 1973 Fiat 128 to a Chevy dealer that I knew was a dog, I had already tried many dealers who knew better but the Chevy dealer must of had some new people. So, perhaps I deserved the Fiero shafting. I do have another trans to put in, three other Fieros and another life (completely Fiero oriented). I will change the trans someday but have other cars to drive and really want to put in a V-8 while its apart.<P>Good luck with your Fiero and don't put it in front of your wife and children. Take it from someone who knows what you will miss most.<P>Robert ||||reg||1
Z||000048||BOILERMAKER||11-26-2001||09:11 AM||||TRIAD, sorry to hear about your problems.  You have mail.<P>Monkeyman, you should be the last person complaining about receiving money from someone who owes you.||||reg||1
Z||000049||TRiAD||11-26-2001||10:40 AM||||Yeah, sorry to say this here, but the Fiero is not anywhere near the top of my list...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Boilermaker, got your email and replied, but I wasn't sure who you were. hehe. <P>Laters...||||reg||1
Z||000050||JohnnyK||11-26-2001||12:43 PM||||Slyguy: So you agree.. The master cylinder is part of the hydraulics.. Of course there is air in there.. The thing is, it had to GET in there in the first place, through the hydraulics.. Broken seal, line, something really small and not noticeable.||||reg||1
